      "title": "Actual PBPS centered root order and bounded inverse",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
        "edition": "arXiv:2609.06905v1; Lean4.33.0/fixedMathlib",
        "anchor": "PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 AppendixB15, genuine next B16 consumer; C2/C3/C4; exact original C2 and both Hessian bounds, eta cap; D1 real Hilbert order.",
        "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
        "attribution": "Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang; attributed printed B15 centered-root order with ASTIS internal construction of the actual quantitative bounded inverse."
      },
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive operator Γ on the real scalar-valued L² space with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. There is q∈L²(ν;ℝ) equal to one ν-almost everywhere, with Tq=q and ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for every u. Set q_P=e q and H_P^0=ker⟨q_P,·⟩, with its inherited Hilbert structure. Membership is exactly zero ν-mean after e⁻¹. The SAME Γ_P annihilates q_P. Put γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη)>0. There exists Γ_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 equal under inclusion to the restriction of Γ_P, positive with Γ_0−γ I positive. Γ_0 is a unit in the algebra of bounded real operators. There exists a bounded real Inv on this SAME centered space with Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. All probability, normalization, range, root, centering, spectral-gap, unit and inverse facts are internally derived from the original inputs; none is an additional public premise. αη=1 and rank-zero E remain legal. No inverse on full H_P is asserted.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel base E with canonical volume, including the disclosed rank-zero extension; V is C²; 0<α≤β; both global Hessian bounds; η>0 and βη≤1.",
        "Canonical normalized laws/kernel, onto pullback e, SAME U/T, full and centered roots, exact centering, gap, unit and bounded inverse are conclusions. Conditional actions are per-observable AE. L² is not assumed finite-dimensional.",
        "γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη); the inverse acts only on H_P^0=ker⟨e1,·⟩ with inherited Hilbert structure; the legal endpoint αη=1 is retained."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Actual PBPS centered root order and bounded inverse",
          "tex": "\\Gamma_0\\ge\\gamma I,\\quad\\gamma=\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}{1+\\alpha\\eta}>0,\\quad\\mathrm{Inv}\\Gamma_0=\\Gamma_0\\mathrm{Inv}=I,\\quad\\|\\mathrm{Inv}\\|\\le\\gamma^{-1}."
        }
      ],
